idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  唇齿相依 | chún chǐ xiāng yī | as close as lips and teeth; mutually interdependent
  咬紧牙关 | yǎo jǐn yá guān | bite teeth tightly; grit teeth and endure hardship
  唇亡齿寒 | chún wáng chǐ hán | if lips are gone teeth get cold; when one falls the other suffers
  伶牙俐齿 | líng yá lì chǐ | clever tongue and sharp teeth; eloquent and glib

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  牙 | yá | tooth; ivory; tusk | diente; colmillo; marfil | 牙 | tooth / tusk | 牙 (interlocking molars or curved tusks) | "" | 4 | 单一结构 | Ancient bronze pictogram representing interlocking animal molars or curved ivory tusks with interlocking hooks. | The curved, interlocking ivory tusk of a great wild beast hooks upward into view (牙). | El colmillo curvado y entrelazado de una bestia milenaria que se curva con fuerza (牙). | 35 | MVH | 
  齿 | chǐ | tooth; age; speak of | diente; dentadura; edad | 齿 | tooth / age | 止 (zhǐ, foot / phonetic) | 口 (mouth with row of teeth) | 8 | 上下结构 | Simplified from traditional 齒. Ancient oracle bone pictogram showing a gaping mouth with an exposed row of teeth. | Open the mouth wide to reveal a neat, sturdy row of biting white teeth (齿). | Abrir la boca de par en par para mostrar la hilera de dientes blancos y firmes (齿). | 214 | YMYB | 齒

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: The sharp curved tusks (牙) combined with the neat rows of biting teeth in the mouth (齿) form human dental teeth (牙齿).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Los afilados colmillos (牙) combinados con la hilera de piezas dentales (齿) componen la dentadura (牙齿).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In classical Chinese anatomy, 牙 originally denoted large rear molars and animal tusks (象牙), while 齿 denoted the front incisors and human teeth. Together, 牙齿 forms the modern collective noun for human and animal dentition.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by dipping 3rd tone: 'yá chǐ' (35-214). Elevate the pitch on 'yá' before letting 'chǐ' dip into low vocal fry.

