semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 牙齿 is the complete, standard noun for physical human or animal teeth, while 牙 alone is used in set compounds and idioms.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 牙齿 vs. 牙 | yá | 牙齿 is the formal and full anatomical noun (刷牙齿, 保护牙齿), whereas 牙 is a flexible monosyllable used in compound terms and daily verbs (刷牙, 牙医, 门牙).
    2 | 牙齿 vs. 象牙 | xiàngyá | 牙齿 refers generally to ordinary teeth, whereas 象牙 designates the valuable, curved ivory tusks of an elephant.
    3 | 牙齿 vs. 齿轮 | chǐlún | 牙齿 is biological dentition, whereas 齿轮 refers to mechanical gearwheels with interlocking cog teeth.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 洁白健康的牙齿不仅关乎个人的形象与自信，更直接影响着食物的消化吸收与身体健康。在日常生活中注重口腔卫生，定期进行牙科检查，是在岁月的流转中留住灿烂笑容与健康体魄的最好方式。 | Jiébái jiànkāng de yáchǐ bùjǐn guānhū gèrén de xíngxiàng yǔ zìxìn, gèng zhíjiē yǐngxiǎng zhe shíwù de xiāohuà xīshōu yǔ shēntǐ jiànkāng. Zài rìcháng shēnghuó zhōng zhùzhòng kǒuqiāng wèishēng, dìngqī jìnxíng yákē jiǎnchá, shì zài suìyuè de liúzhuǎn zhōng liúzhù cànlàn xiàoróng yǔ jiànkāng tǐpò de zuì hǎo fāngshì. | Gleaming white, healthy teeth not only influence personal image and confidence, but directly impact digestion, nutrient absorption, and bodily health. Caring for oral hygiene and scheduling regular dental checkups is the best way to preserve bright smiles across passing years. | Unos dientes blancos y sanos no solo realzan la imagen y la seguridad en uno mismo, sino que condicionan la digestión y el bienestar general. Cuidar la higiene bucal y acudir con regularidad al odontólogo es la mejor forma de conservar una sonrisa radiante a lo largo de los años.
  #2 | 在古生物学研究中，动物的牙齿化石是最能经受岁月侵蚀的珍贵地质凭证。通过微观结构分析与同位素测定，科学家能够从细小的古生物牙齿中精准推断出千万年前古气候变迁以及动物的演化谱系。 | Zài gǔshēngwùxué yánjiū zhōng, dòngwù de yáchǐ huàshí shì zuì néng jīngshòu suìyuè qīnshí de zhēnguì dìzhì píngzhèng. Tōngguò wēiguān jiégòu fēnxī yǔ tóngwèisù cèdìng, kēxuéjiā nénggòu cóng xìxiǎo de gǔshēngwù yáchǐ zhōng jīngzhǔn tuīduàn chū qiānwàn nián qián gǔqìhòu biànqiān yǐjí dòngwù de yǎnhuà pǔxì. | In paleontology, fossilized teeth are the most resilient geological evidence enduring millennia of erosion. Through microstructure and isotopic analysis, scientists can accurately deduce paleoclimate shifts and evolutionary lineages from ancient animal teeth. | En paleontología, los dientes fosilizados son los testimonios geológicos más resistentes a la erosión del tiempo. Mediante el análisis microscópico e isotópico de estas piezas, los científicos infieren con exactitud cambios climáticos remotos y linajes evolutivos milenarios.
